You feel spoiled.

When you zap a wand of polymorph at an object lying on the ground, the 
object will change to a different object in the same class (ie, weapons
remain weapons, potions remain potions, etc).  If you pile a bunch of stuff
up on the same square before zapping the wand, everything in the pile will
change.  That's polypiling.

Careful, though.  Recent versions of Nethack have included `balancers' to
balance the power polypiling gives.  First, some objects in the pile will 
disappear instead of polymorphing (put x objects on a square, zap a wand
of polymorph at the pile, recount the objects.  There will be fewer than
x objects left).  Second, wands of wishing and magic lamps won't ever be
formed by polypiling.  Third, sometimes golems will be formed out of some
of the items in the pile.  The type of golem seems to be determined by the
predominant material in the pile (stone golems from piles with lots of 
rocs, wood golems from piles with lots of wands and/or wooden weapons, 
iron golems from piles with lots of metal).

